     "page": 2,
     "text": "** \nGerald reports consuming approximately eight alcoholic drinks per week.\n\n**Family History:** \n- **Mother:** \n Experienced a myocardial infarction at the age of 64 and is currently alive at 82 years old.\n\n**Assessment Summary:** \nGerald Perez is a 68-year-old male with a controlled history of musculoskeletal injury and GERD. His current include cyclobenzaprine and ibuprofen for the musculoskeletal injury and omeprazole and pantoprazole for GERD management. Vital signs, weight, and exam findings have remained within normal limits over the past few years. He has a significant family history of myocardial infarction, which is pertinent to his cardiovascular risk profile.\n\n**Plan:** \nContinue current medication regimen for musculoskeletal injury and GERD. Schedule routine follow-up appointments to monitor symptoms and adjust treatment as necessary. Encourage lifestyle modifications to further manage GERD, such as avoiding trigger foods and maintaining a healthy weight. Regular monitoring of blood pressure and weight is recommended.\n\n**Conclusion:** \nGerald Perez is effectively managing his musculoskeletal injury and GERD with prescribed medications. His current health status, as evidenced by clinical findings and exam results, indicates stable and well-controlled conditions. Continuous monitoring and adherence to the treatment plan are essential for maintaining his health and preventing complications.\n\n---\n\n**Attending Physician:** \n**Dr. Andrew Johnson, MD** \n**Specialty:** Family Medicine \n**Practice:** Gonzalez Ltd Clinic\n"
